 define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/init(from:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"init(from:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Decoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Decodes the form ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"text":" writes, throwing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DecodingError.dataCorrupted"},{"text":" for a negative","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"vertex count, storage over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix.maximumDecodedWordCountKey"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s limit (two planes’ words), a vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out of range, a side not strictly ascending, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sources"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"targets","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lengths."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(from:)","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(from:)"}}}